From f454a3ed2bcc3795efee3c28380e52aa1aa34e9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:38:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(watch): look at the root itself so a lost root is
 recorded on every platform

MissedReason::RootGone was recorded only when the backend reported the
root's own removal. inotify does; ReadDirectoryChangesW never reports
the watched directory, so on Windows a watcher whose root was removed
answered as a quiet tree and Health::Watching vouched for a tree nobody
watched. A root replaced by another directory at the same path, by a
rename away and a new directory, was recorded on no platform and a
reconciliation cleared the state back to Watching.

TreeWatcher now records which directory its root is (device and inode
on unix, none elsewhere) and looks at the root's path without following
a link: on every next_batch, including a call where nothing arrived,
and in mark_reconciled. A root that cannot be looked at, is not a
directory, is a link, or is another directory records RootGone once and
for good. mark_reconciled refuses a watcher whose root is gone, so it is
replaced, not reconciled, like a stopped one. The accumulator is told
when the root is already held gone so a removal the backend reports as
well is not counted again, in that batch or a later one.

Module doc, MissedReason::RootGone, mark_reconciled and next_batch say
what changed. Five new tests; no existing test is touched.

Ticket: ORI-T-0163
Spec: ARCHITECTURE.md#5-data-flows
