+/// The device and inode of a directory, where the platform has them.
+///
+/// `std` gives a file's identity on unix only; on Windows the stable `std` has
+/// none, so the root there is told from its replacement by nothing but being
+/// a directory at the same path. `hooks.rs` does the same for a file.
+#[cfg(unix)]
