From d31679bf37e1c4922f1978efbdcb7e88d1b47ad4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:46:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(watch): deliver a loss mark_reconciled finds, always
 list a lost root

A review of the look at the root found that a loss mark_reconciled finds
was held in the health and never reached a batch: the backend's own
report was dropped as already known, so a consumer of Batch::missed was
never told. TreeWatcher now remembers the discovery and the next batch
lists RootGone, even when nothing else arrived, without recording it in
the health again. The module doc and the docs of MissedChanges, Health
and mark_reconciled now say every loss is delivered in the next batch,
and every loss but RootGone is held until a reconciliation clears it.

RootGone is exempt from the cap on a missed state's reasons, so sixteen
other causes cannot push it out, and a RootGone already listed is not
counted again, so two reports in one window count once.

On Windows a root deleted while the backend's handle on it is open stays
delete-pending: still listed in its parent, so std's metadata passes it,
but not openable. The look now also opens the root there, with backup
semantics and no access, and an open that fails reads as gone.

Also: the docs say the look does not follow a link at the root itself,
that a replaced root is not told apart on Windows, that on ext4 an
immediate rm -rf and mkdir often reuses the inode, that FSEvents watches
a path and not a directory, and what next_batch's None does and does not
mean. Six new tests; no existing test is touched.

